WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:02.950
Alright guys, we’re on the road!

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:04.370
Wooo!

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:18.420
How are you guys feeling?

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:19.480
Great, great, great.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.860
So we were pulling out at like
7:30 in the morning

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:27.340
and my feeling as we’re pulling out was,

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.660
“Are we really doing this?” I mean it just 
seemed very unbelievable to me

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.760
that it was actually happening.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.949
Affirmative Art is a way of projecting 
the future by drawing or painting it.

00:00:43.949 --> 00:00:48.689
This idea of acknowledging each 
person and their right to dream

00:00:48.689 --> 00:00:50.540
and to achieve their own purpose,

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:55.440
is the first step in a more communal
vision for a shared world.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:08.340
We are painting the tour van. 
It’s the launch day of the tour.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.660
We’re leaving tomorrow from…from Boston

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:14.700
and then heading to New
York to Harlem

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.400
and then we will end the tour in LA.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:21.780
It’s exciting. It’s also sort of a
big responsibility

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.380
because we are engaging so 
many different communities,

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:28.480
but it’s also appreciation for having reached this far.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:44.080
It was so fast paced that you know we
would drive in the morning,

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.580
and then we would do a workshop in the afternoon.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:49.760
We saw the U.S. but we really only saw it

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:53.200
through the lens of these particular community spaces.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.300
You just got to meet people

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:56.840
and just have conversations with them.

